  "Question": "\\([x-(y-x)]-[(x-y)-x]=\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2y\\)",
    "B": "\\(2x\\)",
    "C": "\\(-2y\\)",
    "D": "\\(-2x\\)",
    "E": "\\(0\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "A minus sign before parentheses reverses the sign of every enclosed term. Simplify each bracket first, then subtract:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n[x-(y-x)]-[(x-y)-x]\n&=(x-y+x)-(x-y-x)\\\\\n&=(2x-y)-(-y)\\\\\n&=2x-y+y\\\\\n&=2x.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{2x}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
